WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.033
-In his state of the union
address this week,

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:06.033
President Biden made a point
to focus on kitchen table issues

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:08.934
that impact ordinary Americans,
like junk fees,

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:11.467
prescription drug costs,
and even concert prices.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.267
And then yesterday,
House Republicans,

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.567
led by their de facto speaker,
Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:17.467
decided to respond
by focusing on an issue

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.300
that really matters
to Americans --

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.968
why did Twitter censor
Hunter Biden's nudes?

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.300
[ Laughter ]
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.033
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:31.167
Say what you want about Biden,
but on Tuesday,

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.801
he made a clear choice
to focus on economic populism

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.400
as the predominant theme
of his speech.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.400
He talked about everything

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.167
from breaking up
big tech monopolies

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.033
to capping the price
of insulin,

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:42.200
eliminating junk fees
at hotels and airlines,

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.267
and even cracking down

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.200
on inflated ticket prices
for concerts.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.100
Look, I don't know for sure,
but I'm starting to think

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.801
Joe Biden might be
a secret Swiftie,

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:50.734
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]
just sitting at his computer,

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:54.767
just refreshing Ticketmaster
over and over again.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:57.000
"Mr. President, we need you
in the Situation Room!"

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.267
Hold your horses.
I'm number 8,000 in the queue.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.901
[ Laughter and applause ]
I think I --

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:02.100
I think I got a shot.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.234
Oh, Taylor,
look what you made me do.

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:05.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:08.133
In fact, there were even times
when it seemed like Biden

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:11.000
was maybe taking some rhetorical
flourishes from Donald Trump,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.267
but, instead of just talking
out of his ass, like Trump does,

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.667
[ Laughter ]
Biden was backing it up
with actual policy.

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:18.300
-Tonight, I'm announcing
new standards require

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.434
all construction materials used

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:22.868
in federal
infrastructure projects

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:24.734
to be made in America.

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:25.767
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:27.734
And, on my watch,
American roads, bridges,

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.100
and American highways
are going to be made

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.133
with American products as well.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.734
My economic plan is
about investing

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:35.634
in places and people
that have been forgotten.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:38.334
Too many people
have been left behind

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.200
and treated like
they're invisible.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.133
Outside of Columbus, Ohio,
Intel is building

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:46.901
semiconductor factories
on 1,000 acres.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.834
Last year, I cracked down,
on behalf of many of you,

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:51.267
on foreign shipping companies

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:52.968
that were making you
pay higher prices

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:55.033
for every good coming
into the country.

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.901
[ Cheering and applause ]
Americans are tired of being --

00:01:57.901 --> 00:02:00.467
we're tired of being played
for suckers.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.400
-Biden basically took Trump's
rhetorical schtick,

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.067
but backed it up
with actual legislation.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.701
He even released it
as a single, called...

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:10.501
The other difference is
Biden did it

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:12.601
without going on a bunch
of insane tangents

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:14.701
and exaggerating how many jobs
he was creating.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.033
If that had been Trump,
that speech would've
been twice as long

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:19.133
and he would've gone
off-script after every line.

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.300
[ As Trump ]
Intel is building
a factory in Ohio.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.701
They were going
to build it in China,

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:25.634
but then I became president
and I called up the CEO.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:27.400
His name is Chip, Chip Intel.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.968
[ Laughter ]
And I said, I said, "Mr. Intel,

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:31.701
you better build that factory
in Columbus."

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:33.634
Columbus! We love Columbus,
don't we?

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:34.534
[ Laughter ]
We love it.

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:35.467
Named after the great

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.067
film director Chris Columbus.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:38.701
[ Laughter ]
He made -- He made the movie

00:02:38.701 --> 00:02:40.501
"Home Alone 2:
Lost in New York,"

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.901
[ Laughter ]
a movie I originally --
I originally starred in.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:43.901
They cut most of my scenes.

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.067
It was very sad.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.467
I remember a guy named Marv
came up to me.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.367
[ Laughter ]
Big guy, tall guy,
tears in his eyes,

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:52.300
iron print on his face,
and he said to me,

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.167
[ Laughter ]
"You got to help us catch
this little [bleep]."

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:56.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:57.534
And, in particular,

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.300
Biden focused
on a bunch of real problems

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.868
that people face every day,
like, for example,

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:04.868
the high cost of essential
medications or hidden fees.

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:08.901
-We capped the cost of insulin
at $35 a month

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.367
[ Cheering and applause ]
for seniors on Medicare.

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:11.734
Let's cap the cost of insulin

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:14.501
for everybody at $35.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:17.634
My administration is also
taking on junk fees.

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:21.434
We're making airlines show you
the full ticket price up front.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.868
We've reduced exorbitant
bank overdrafts.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:29.501
[ Applause ]
We're cutting credit card
late fees by 75%.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:32.200
We're going to ban surprise
resort fees

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.834
that hotels charge on your bill.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:36.601
[ Applause ]
We can stop service fees

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:39.200
on tickets to concerts
and sporting events

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.234
and make companies disclose
all the fees up front.

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:45.167
And we'll prohibit airlines
from charging $50 round trip

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:48.601
for family just to be able
to sit together.

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:50.767
[ Applause ]
Baggage fees are bad enough.

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:54.501
Airlines can't treat your child
like a piece of baggage.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.634
-Drug prices,
Internet companies, junk fees.

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:58.868
He basically took everything
grandpas complain about

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.067
and turned it into a speech.

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:01.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:03.100
[ As Biden ]
Why do they make thermostats

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.567
that go all the way up to 77°?

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:07.000
[ Laughter ]
Folks, we're going
to cap it at 68°

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.734
and I'm mailing every American
a sweater.

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:11.067
[ Laughter and applause ]
Another idea from that list

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.601
that I think most people
can probably get behind is

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:14.834
capping service fees on concerts
and sporting events.

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:16.601
I mean, we all hate it
when you click buy

00:04:16.601 --> 00:04:18.367
on some tickets
that say they're 100 bucks,

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:19.767
but then, by the time
you get to checkout,

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:21.501
they're double the price,
after you count up all the fees

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:22.767
and a lot of them
don't even seem real.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:23.601
It's like...

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:39.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:39.734 --> 00:04:41.601
So, that's the kind of thing

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:44.467
Biden was focused on
in his speech on Tuesday.

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:46.100
Of course, you'll probably
also recall

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.367
the GOP heckled him
for claiming some Republicans,

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:50.400
like Senators Ron Johnson
and Rick Scott,

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.000
want to cut Social Security
and Medicare.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.667
Scott and Johnson
both proposed plans

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:55.467
to sunset
all federal legislation,

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:57.367
which would include
Social Security and Medicare,

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:59.801
and require periodic votes
to renew them.

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.901
Right now,
those programs are mandatory,

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.300
but Johnson and Scott proposed

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.801
putting them up
for vote every five years.

00:05:05.801 --> 00:05:07.434
Or, in Johnson's case,
every year.

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:08.801
And yet,
when Biden brought it up,

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:10.067
Republicans,
like Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:11.400
called him a liar.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.400
-Instead of making the wealthy
pay their fair share,

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.033
some Republicans --

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:18.534
some Republicans want Medicare
and Social Security to sunset.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:19.968
I'm not saying it's a majority.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:23.567
[ Booing ]

00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:25.434
Let me give you --

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:27.567
Anybody who doubts it,

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:29.200
contact my office.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.033
I'll give you a copy.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.033
I'll give you a copy

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:34.400
of the proposal.
-You're a liar!

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.367
-That means Congress
doesn't vote --

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:38.300
[ Shouting ]
-Liar!

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.868
-I'm not saying
it's a majority of you.

00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:40.901
I don't even think it's even

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:42.400
a significant --
-Don't speak anymore.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.601
[ Shouting ]

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:46.767
-But it's being proposed
by individuals.

00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:48.601
I'm politely not naming them,

00:05:48.601 --> 00:05:50.634
but it's being proposed
by some of you.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.767
-I like Biden's
passive-aggressive grandpa move

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:54.667
of "I'm politely
not naming them."

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:56.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:57.934
[ As Biden ]
Look, I'm not going to say
who they are,

00:05:57.934 --> 00:05:59.467
but one guy's named
after a penis

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:00.701
and the other looks like one.

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:02.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:03.667
Then yesterday --

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:06.300
yesterday, Biden showed up
at a speech in Wisconsin

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.234
with physical proof
of the Republican proposals

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.067
he had cited
from Johnson and Scott

00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:11.801
to cut Medicare
and Social Security.

00:06:11.801 --> 00:06:14.200
-We've had a spirited debate
last night [ Mirthless chuckle ]

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.934
with my Republican friends.

00:06:15.934 --> 00:06:18.067
They seemed shocked...

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:19.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:22.834
...when I raised the plans
of some of their members

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:26.234
and their caucus
to cut Social Security.

00:06:26.234 --> 00:06:28.501
And Marjorie Taylor Greene
and others stood up and said,

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:30.300
"Liar, liar."

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.334
Well, guess what.

00:06:32.334 --> 00:06:34.934
You know, I remind you
that Rick Scott, from Florida,

00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:38.367
the guy who ran the U.S. Senate
campaign, has a plan.

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:40.801
I got his brochure right here.

00:06:40.801 --> 00:06:42.968
[ Laughter ]
Has a plan.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:44.300
Here's what he says
in this plan.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.334
Let me open it up here.
Sorry.

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:49.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:52.801
He says, "All federal
legislation sunsets

00:06:52.801 --> 00:06:54.367
every five years.

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:59.234
If a law is worth keeping,
Congress can pass it again."

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:01.901
Social Security and Medicare,
Medicaid.

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:04.734
Ron Johnson on Social Security
and Medicare --

00:07:04.734 --> 00:07:08.701
"We should transfer everything

00:07:08.701 --> 00:07:12.534
so we have to consider
everything every year."

00:07:12.534 --> 00:07:16.434
-Now, I do get nervous whenever
Biden tries to use props.

00:07:16.434 --> 00:07:17.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.934 --> 00:07:20.100
It's like when you sit down
next to an old guy on a plane

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.234
and he wants
to show you pictures

00:07:21.234 --> 00:07:22.667
of the Thunderbird on his phone.

00:07:22.667 --> 00:07:24.901
[ Gravelly voice ]
I had this baby since '62.

00:07:24.901 --> 00:07:26.901
Hold on.
Let me -- Ah.

00:07:26.901 --> 00:07:28.601
How do I close out
a Candy Crush?

00:07:28.601 --> 00:07:30.534
Hold on. Ah!
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:31.968
Oh, now the flashlight's on.

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:34.501
Oh, oh, oh, here we go.
Oh, goddamn it!

00:07:34.501 --> 00:07:36.267
That's my niece.
I called her by accident.

00:07:36.267 --> 00:07:37.567
Hi, honey!

00:07:37.567 --> 00:07:39.968
Hi. I'm with a nice man
on the plane, honey.

00:07:39.968 --> 00:07:42.400
I got to go.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.901
So, that's what Biden's
been focused on.

00:07:43.901 --> 00:07:46.033
House Republicans, meanwhile,
held a hearing yesterday

00:07:46.033 --> 00:07:48.567
that I guess was supposed to be
about censorship on Twitter,

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:50.667
but, in reality, it was just
an opportunity to whine

00:07:50.667 --> 00:07:53.133
about how their personal
Twitter accounts were treated

00:07:53.133 --> 00:07:55.200
before new owner Elon Musk
took over.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.100
Colorado Congresswoman
Lauren Boebert, for example,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.901
yelled at a bunch
of former Twitter executives

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:01.334
about why her personal Twitter
account had been censored.

00:08:01.334 --> 00:08:02.868
Now, I would like you
to watch this clip

00:08:02.868 --> 00:08:05.200
and try to decide whether
you're watching an actual adult

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.033
[ Laughter ]
at an actual
congressional hearing

00:08:07.033 --> 00:08:09.400
or a high school sophomore
yelling at a friend

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:10.767
in the hallway after class.

00:08:10.767 --> 00:08:13.334
-Did either of you approve
the shadow banning

00:08:13.334 --> 00:08:16.167
of my account, @laurenboebert?

00:08:16.167 --> 00:08:19.000
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:19.801
Yes or no?

00:08:19.801 --> 00:08:21.501
-No, I did not.

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:23.033
-Not to the best
of my recollection.

00:08:23.033 --> 00:08:24.000
-I'll ask again.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:24.934
[ Laughter ]
Did you shadow ban

00:08:24.934 --> 00:08:27.467
my account, yes or no?

00:08:27.467 --> 00:08:29.133
-Again, not to the best
of my recollection.

00:08:29.133 --> 00:08:31.200
-The answer is, Mr. Roth,
yes, you did!

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.567
I found out last night
from Twitter staff

00:08:33.567 --> 00:08:37.567
that you suppressed my account
for this tweet.

00:08:37.567 --> 00:08:39.634
[ Laughter ]
It's a freaking joke

00:08:39.634 --> 00:08:41.934
about Hillary Clinton
being angry

00:08:41.934 --> 00:08:44.400
that she couldn't rig
her election!

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:46.734
It's a joke!
But in response,

00:08:46.734 --> 00:08:50.801
being the sinister overlords
that you all are,

00:08:50.801 --> 00:08:55.734
you placed a 90-day account
filter so I could not be found.

00:08:55.734 --> 00:08:57.434
You silenced me
from communicating

00:08:57.434 --> 00:09:01.434
with the American people
over a freaking joke!

00:09:01.434 --> 00:09:04.467
Now, who the hell do you think
that you are?

00:09:04.467 --> 00:09:05.834
[ Laughter ]

00:09:05.834 --> 00:09:08.767
-[ As Boebert ]
It was a freaking joke,
Kayleigh!

00:09:08.767 --> 00:09:09.934
[ Laughter ]
Okay?

00:09:09.934 --> 00:09:13.033
I said it's cool
you won prom queen,

00:09:13.033 --> 00:09:15.701
even though you're already
the queen of Bitchistan...

00:09:15.701 --> 00:09:16.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:16.934 --> 00:09:19.868
...as a freaking joke.

00:09:19.868 --> 00:09:21.601
You overlord!

00:09:21.601 --> 00:09:25.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.400
Then there was
the other Boebert,

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:27.434
Marjorie Taylor Greene...
[ Laughter ]

00:09:27.434 --> 00:09:29.133
...who similarly used her time

00:09:29.133 --> 00:09:30.667
to scold former
Twitter employees

00:09:30.667 --> 00:09:32.234
for suspending her personal
Twitter account

00:09:32.234 --> 00:09:33.534
after she repeatedly lied

00:09:33.534 --> 00:09:35.067
and spread
dangerous misinformation

00:09:35.067 --> 00:09:36.767
about the pandemic
and the COVID vaccine.

00:09:36.767 --> 00:09:38.467
Now, just a quick warning
about this clip.

00:09:38.467 --> 00:09:40.200
Don't stare directly
into her eyes,

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:43.534
[ Laughter ]
unless you're covering your eyes
with lead-lined oven mitts.

00:09:43.534 --> 00:09:46.501
[ Laughter ]
-You can consider your speech
canceled during my time

00:09:46.501 --> 00:09:48.767
because you canceled mine.

00:09:48.767 --> 00:09:52.901
You see, you permanently banned
my personal Twitter account

00:09:52.901 --> 00:09:55.434
and it was my campaign
account, also.

00:09:55.434 --> 00:09:57.868
January 2, 2002,

00:09:57.868 --> 00:10:01.834
you permanently banned
my Twitter account.

